 The prompt builder treats point tags as ordinary text, so they reach the model unchanged.
 Pacing also follows the reference clip and the punctuation.
+
+## Long-form replies
+
+```sh
+tensorfold serve DRAMA3_DIR --voices voices/ --default-voice NAME --long-form
+```
+
+With `--long-form`, a speech input longer than `--long-form-chars` (default 300 code points) is spoken in segments instead of in one synthesis. Each segment hears the segments before it: the earlier segments' text and generated codes are added as references after the request's references and the voice's, with the latest last. This follows the way Fish's long-form inference keeps earlier segments in context.
+
+- **Segments.** The input is cut at sentence ends (`.` `!` `?` `…` followed by white space, keeping closing quotes and brackets) and at line breaks. Sentences are packed greedily up to the limit. A sentence longer than the limit is cut at `;` `:` `,`, then at spaces, then anywhere.
+- **History.** `--long-form-history K` (0 to 3, default 1) sets how many earlier segments a segment hears. The oldest is dropped when the prompt would exceed the engine's prompt limit.
+- **Audio.** The segments' audio is joined with no added silence: the pauses at the joins are the model's own.
+- **Seeds.** Each segment's seed comes from its own prompt rows, as a single synthesis's does.
+- **Limits.**
+  - More than 12 segments are refused up front.
+  - A reply may use 6000 frames in all; each segment gets at most what is left.
+  - A segment that is clipped (by the engine's frame limit or the budget) ends the reply, and its audio is kept.
+- **Response headers.** `X-Finish-Reason` is `stop` only when every segment stopped by itself. `X-Long-Form-Segments: N;S2,S3,…` gives the number of segments spoken and the sample offset at which each segment after the first starts.
+- **Streaming.** With `stream: true` the segments stream in order; first audio arrives after segment 1. Both headers come as trailers, declared by `Trailer: X-Finish-Reason, X-Long-Form-Segments`.
+
+An input that fits in one segment, and every request when `--long-form` is off, is served exactly as before.
